course: dictionary
lesson: 4447
title: Handy: useful, close, or clever with hands
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Handy has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one to use. Read the words around it and ask: is it about being useful, being close by, or being good with your hands?
explain: «A handy trick to practise it: say "k", then slide back into a soft, breathy scrape.» Here handy means useful and easy to use. Test it by swapping in useful: "a useful trick" still makes sense.
explain: «Keep a torch handy» means keep it near and easy to reach, so you can grab it fast. The phrase «come in handy» means be useful later. When you meet handy, check the clues before you pick a meaning.
fact: Handy means useful and easy to use, as in «a handy tip».
fact: Handy can also mean near and easy to reach, as in «handy for the shops».
fact: Handy can mean good at doing things with your hands.
fact: «Come in handy» means be useful later.
fact: «Small handy ships» describes ships that are useful and easy to use.
exercise: «A handy trick to practise it: say "k", then slide back into a soft, breathy scrape.» What does handy mean here? | Hard to find | *Useful and easy to use | Dirty and wet | Very large
exercise: «Keep a torch handy» means what? | *Keep it near and easy to reach | Keep it locked in a cupboard | Keep it under the bed for ever | Keep it far away in a box
exercise: Mum says, «This will come in handy later.» What does come in handy mean? | Arrive late | Be given away now | *Be useful later | Be broken
test: «Handy for the shops» means the shops are what? | *Close by and easy to reach | Full of toys | Closed on Sundays | Far away across the sea
test: Which sentence uses handy to mean good with your hands? | The pen is handy for the dog | The bus was handy and late | The tap is handy and blue | *Ben is handy at fixing bikes
exam: Jayden says, «The caravels were handy ships.» Which meaning fits best? | Painted bright red | *Useful and easy to use | Hidden under the sea | Very tall and thin
